      {
        "blocks": [
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "Using delimited blocks, you can nest blocks inside of one other. (Blocks can also be nested inside sections, list items, and table cells, which is a separate topic)."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "First, the parent block must have the compound content model. The compound content model means that the block’s content is a sequence of zero or more blocks."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "When nesting a block that uses a different structural container from the parent, it’s enough to ensure that the child block is entirely inside the parent block. Delimited blocks cannot be interleaved."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "listing",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "====\nHere's a sample AsciiDoc document:\n\n----\n= Document Title\nAuthor Name\n\nContent goes here.\n----\n\nThe document header is useful, but not required.\n===="
              }
            ],
            "language": "asciidoc",
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "When nesting a delimited block that uses the same structural container, it’s necessary to vary the length of the delimiter lines (i.e., make the length of the delimiter lines for the child block different than the length of the delimiter lines for the parent block). Varying the delimiter line length allows the parser to distinguish one block from another."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "listing",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "====\nHere are your options:\n\n.Red Pill\n[%collapsible]\n======\nEscape into the real world.\n======\n\n.Blue Pill\n[%collapsible]\n======\nLive within the simulated reality without want or fear.\n======\n===="
              }
            ],
            "language": "asciidoc",
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "The delimiter length for the nested structural container can either be shorter or longer than the parent. That’s a personal style choice."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          }
        ],
        "context": "section",
        "id": "nesting",
        "level": 1,
        "roles": [],
        "title": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "Nesting blocks"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
